{"vid":"Cp0-Yu31uJ4","source":"Cp0-Yu31uJ4.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.4,"txt":"AI is supposed to make work faster and"},{"t":2.4,"txt":"easier, but some experts say it's also"},{"t":4.3,"txt":"causing unforeseen and sometimes"},{"t":6.3,"txt":"overlooked challenges for employees. A"},{"t":9,"txt":"survey found that 74% of the C-suite"},{"t":11.5,"txt":"reported feeling excited about AI, while"},{"t":14,"txt":"68% of individual contributors reported"},{"t":16.3,"txt":"feeling anxious or overwhelmed. Dennis"},{"t":18.6,"txt":"Stoly, the head of applied psychology at"},{"t":20.8,"txt":"the American Psychological Association,"},{"t":22.9,"txt":"says there's a disconnect between the"},{"t":24.3,"txt":"expected benefits of AI and employees'"},{"t":26.5,"txt":"actual experiences. Experts say there"},{"t":28.8,"txt":"are a few reasons why some employees are"},{"t":30.4,"txt":"feeling overwhelmed by having to use AI"},{"t":32.2,"txt":"in their workplaces."},{"t":33.4,"txt":">> [music]"},{"t":33.8,"txt":">> First, some workers say they're losing"},{"t":35.8,"txt":"time checking and fixing AI outputs. A"},{"t":38.4,"txt":"majority of employees said that using AI"},{"t":40.4,"txt":"at work has saved them between 1 and 7"},{"t":42.6,"txt":"hours each week, according to a survey"},{"t":44.3,"txt":"from Workday. However, employees also"},{"t":46.6,"txt":"reported that they lost 40% of those"},{"t":48.6,"txt":"efficiency gains by having to correct,"},{"t":50.5,"txt":"rewrite, edit, or fact-check"},{"t":52,"txt":"AI-generated content. Sundar Pichai, the"},{"t":54.5,"txt":"CEO of Google, said the AI models are"},{"t":56.6,"txt":"prone to errors and that people should"},{"t":58.2,"txt":"use them alongside other tools."},{"t":60.3,"txt":">> [music]"},{"t":60.4,"txt":">> I spoke with Linda Lee, a technical"},{"t":62.2,"txt":"recruiter, who says that AI saved time"},{"t":64.2,"txt":"on certain tasks, but she estimates that"},{"t":66.2,"txt":"she spent almost half the time she"},{"t":67.6,"txt":"gained correcting and fact-checking the"},{"t":69.2,"txt":"results. For instance, sometimes the AI"},{"t":71.6,"txt":"software rated a candidate's resume as a"},{"t":73.6,"txt":"95% match when it was closer to 30% and"},{"t":76.6,"txt":"also frequently mislabeled strong"},{"t":78.3,"txt":"candidates as a poor match for a job."},{"t":80.6,"txt":"Companies may think that AI is making"},{"t":82.4,"txt":"work faster, but Lee says that any"},{"t":84.4,"txt":"efficiency gains are only possible"},{"t":86,"txt":"because there was a person making sure"},{"t":87.8,"txt":"AI wasn't making mistakes and doing"},{"t":89.8,"txt":"everything behind the scenes. Second,"},{"t":91.9,"txt":"some workers say they've had to learn"},{"t":93.2,"txt":"how to use AI on their own. While many"},{"t":95.5,"txt":"companies are pushing employees to use"},{"t":97.4,"txt":"AI, only 27% of individual contributors"},{"t":100.5,"txt":"said they received company AI training"},{"t":102.5,"txt":"and just 32% reported clear access to AI"},{"t":105.1,"txt":"tools, according to a survey. Employers'"},{"t":107.5,"txt":"expectations around AI can create an"},{"t":109.4,"txt":"unsustainable cycle for workers,"},{"t":111,"txt":"according to Stoly. He says employees"},{"t":113,"txt":"are as busy as they can possibly be"},{"t":114.6,"txt":"during the workday and then they feel"},{"t":116.2,"txt":"like they need to spend their evenings"},{"t":117.5,"txt":"learning about AI so that they can keep"},{"t":119.3,"txt":"up and make the next day even busier."},{"t":120.5,"txt":"[music]"},{"t":121.2,"txt":"Devin Boudreaux, a digital PR strategist"},{"t":123.5,"txt":"based in Boise, Idaho, says that before"},{"t":125.5,"txt":"he could train AI to assist him, he"},{"t":127.4,"txt":"first had to teach himself how to work"},{"t":129,"txt":"with the models. In Boudreaux's view,"},{"t":131.1,"txt":"companies are urging employees to become"},{"t":132.9,"txt":"AI proficient, he says, but they want"},{"t":135,"txt":"you to do it on your own time. Third,"},{"t":137.2,"txt":"using AI tools can cause mental fatigue."},{"t":139.7,"txt":"A recent study from Boston Consulting"},{"t":141.4,"txt":"Group found that workers who frequently"},{"t":143.1,"txt":"use AI experience an increase in mental"},{"t":145.2,"txt":"fatigue, a phenomenon they termed AI"},{"t":147.4,"txt":"brain fry. Those workers are more likely"},{"t":149.7,"txt":"to make mistakes, feel overwhelmed or"},{"t":151.8,"txt":"mentally foggy, and struggle to make"},{"t":153.5,"txt":"decisions. The study found that workers"},{"t":156,"txt":"who use three or more AI agents in their"},{"t":158,"txt":"workflow are more likely to suffer"},{"t":159.4,"txt":"negative effects like mental fog than"},{"t":161.5,"txt":"those who use one or two. And tasks that"},{"t":163.3,"txt":"involve high-levels of oversight require"},{"t":165.2,"txt":"14% more mental effort and cause a 12%"},{"t":168.3,"txt":"increase in mental fatigue. Another"},{"t":170.1,"txt":"major contributor to brain fry is that"},{"t":172,"txt":"AI often increases the depth and breadth"},{"t":174.2,"txt":"of employees' workloads, according to"},{"t":175.9,"txt":"Julie Bedard, a managing director at BCG"},{"t":178.2,"txt":"and a co-author of the study. Even some"},{"t":180.3,"txt":"AI leaders say they're feeling the"},{"t":181.6,"txt":"oversight-related strain. Ben Wigler,"},{"t":183.8,"txt":"co-founder of Lovemind AI, told French"},{"t":186.2,"txt":"news agency AFP that using AI causes a"},{"t":188.7,"txt":"brand new kind of cognitive load"},{"t":190.8,"txt":"stemming from the need to babysit"},{"t":192.2,"txt":"models. Ultimately, Stoly, the head of"},{"t":194.9,"txt":"applied psychology at the American"},{"t":196.5,"txt":"Psychological Association, says the goal"},{"t":198.7,"txt":"of implementing AI at a company should"},{"t":200.6,"txt":"not be to just use more AI. He says the"},{"t":203.1,"txt":"goal has to be creating higher quality"},{"t":205,"txt":"work in a sustainable way so that when"},{"t":207,"txt":"you're 5 years out, you still have a"},{"t":208.5,"txt":"thriving organization filled with happy"},{"t":210.5,"txt":"employees."}],"words":[{"t":0.44,"w":"AI"},{"t":0.76,"w":"is"},{"t":0.92,"w":"supposed"},{"t":1.24,"w":"to"},{"t":1.28,"w":"make"},{"t":1.44,"w":"work"},{"t":1.64,"w":"faster"},{"t":2.2,"w":"and"},{"t":2.4,"w":"easier,"},{"t":2.92,"w":"but"},{"t":3.08,"w":"some"},{"t":3.32,"w":"experts"},{"t":3.72,"w":"say"},{"t":3.92,"w":"it's"},{"t":4.08,"w":"also"},{"t":4.32,"w":"causing"},{"t":4.72,"w":"unforeseen"},{"t":5.56,"w":"and"},{"t":5.68,"w":"sometimes"},{"t":6.28,"w":"overlooked"},{"t":7.04,"w":"challenges"},{"t":7.52,"w":"for"},{"t":7.68,"w":"employees."},{"t":8.96,"w":"A"},{"t":9,"w":"survey"},{"t":9.36,"w":"found"},{"t":9.72,"w":"that"},{"t":9.88,"w":"74%"},{"t":10.76,"w":"of"},{"t":10.84,"w":"the"},{"t":10.92,"w":"C-suite"},{"t":11.48,"w":"reported"},{"t":11.84,"w":"feeling"},{"t":12.16,"w":"excited"},{"t":12.84,"w":"about"},{"t":13.12,"w":"AI,"},{"t":13.72,"w":"while"},{"t":13.96,"w":"68%"},{"t":14.84,"w":"of"},{"t":14.96,"w":"individual"},{"t":15.44,"w":"contributors"},{"t":15.96,"w":"reported"},{"t":16.28,"w":"feeling"},{"t":16.56,"w":"anxious"},{"t":16.96,"w":"or"},{"t":17.12,"w":"overwhelmed."},{"t":18.2,"w":"Dennis"},{"t":18.56,"w":"Stoly,"},{"t":19.24,"w":"the"},{"t":19.36,"w":"head"},{"t":19.6,"w":"of"},{"t":19.68,"w":"applied"},{"t":20,"w":"psychology"},{"t":20.68,"w":"at"},{"t":20.8,"w":"the"},{"t":20.92,"w":"American"},{"t":21.32,"w":"Psychological"},{"t":22,"w":"Association,"},{"t":22.88,"w":"says"},{"t":23.08,"w":"there's"},{"t":23.28,"w":"a"},{"t":23.32,"w":"disconnect"},{"t":23.92,"w":"between"},{"t":24.16,"w":"the"},{"t":24.28,"w":"expected"},{"t":24.8,"w":"benefits"},{"t":25.2,"w":"of"},{"t":25.32,"w":"AI"},{"t":25.88,"w":"and"},{"t":26,"w":"employees'"},{"t":26.48,"w":"actual"},{"t":26.84,"w":"experiences."},{"t":28.04,"w":"Experts"},{"t":28.48,"w":"say"},{"t":28.68,"w":"there"},{"t":28.84